{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"cc714ea573ced272cbeb576a988e9871a9849c3b98bf7c627101d0958b54c72f","digest":{"component_or_area":"review-bot retrigger","key_entities":["retrigger.py","TRIGGER_TOKEN","_TOKEN_RE","_RETIRED_TOKEN_RE","infra/gerrit/gerrit_to_platform.ini.template","post_comment","recheck-review","rerun-llm-review","_ACCEPTED_MESSAGE","_refusal_message","test_review_bot_retrigger.py","test_review_bot.py"],"problem_keywords":["trigger word collision","CI dispatch","substring matching","gerrit chatops","recheck","rerun-llm-review","comment matcher"],"propositions":["Substring-based ChatOps matcher in external lfit/releng-gerrit_to_platform maps 'recheck' to Verified workflow, and the LLM trigger word 'recheck-review' contains 'recheck' as a substring, causing unintended CI dispatch and run cancellations.","The bot's own reply texts embed the retired trigger word verbatim, so bot-posted comments themselves re-dispatch the external CI matcher.","Rename the LLM trigger from 'recheck-review' to 'rerun-llm-review', which shares no substring with any ini-mapped ChatOps key, and implement hard cutover with no deprecation window.","All bot-posted reply texts and documentation must be scrubbed of the retired word; the retired trigger now draws a silent no-op or a refusal comment that describes rather than spells the old word."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787468675461220001,"uuid":"327c0129-e746-482c-b209-27e75da4ab71"}